    "response": "Impact map:\n\n- Payload contract — `src/notifications/jobs/email.job.ts`: `SendEmailJob` currently contains `recipient`, `template`, and `variables`; `locale` belongs here. The repository does not establish locale’s type or requiredness, though a required `locale: string` would match the existing contract style.\n- Producer — `src/notifications/email.producer.ts`: `EmailProducer.enqueue(payload: SendEmailJob)` adds the payload unchanged to the `email` queue as `send-email`. Its `Queue<SendEmailJob>` typing automatically adopts the new field. No upstream `EmailProducer` call sites or email payload constructors exist in this fixture.\n- Consumer — `src/notifications/email.processor.ts`: `EmailProcessor.process(job: Job<SendEmailJob>)` forwards `job.data` unchanged, so locale will reach delivery without processor transformation. `src/notifications/mail-delivery.service.ts`: `MailDeliveryService.send(message: SendEmailJob)` is the terminal consumer; it currently uses only `template` and `recipient`. It must change only if locale should alter delivery behavior—the repository does not define those semantics.\n- Tests — `test/notifications/email.processor.test.ts`: the sole email-flow test builds an inline payload without locale and verifies that the complete `job.data` object reaches `delivery.send`. Its fixture should include locale to cover propagation. Because the job is cast to `never`, the existing test may continue compiling and passing even after locale becomes required, so it does not currently enforce the payload contract. There are no producer or delivery-service tests in the fixture.",
